ACTOR A
   ↓
HIGH CENTRALITY
   ↓
HIGH INFLUENCE

But:

CENTRALITY
≠
AUTHORITY

and:

INFLUENCE
≠
RESPONSIBILITY

A highly connected actor may simply occupy a structurally important position.

R8.89 calls the invalid inference:

CENTRALITY_RESPONSIBILITY_FALLACY

No constitutional classification may rely on it alone.


