XX. 🜂 R8.89 LAW

> Where constitutional effects emerge from interacting actors, relations or structures, causal attribution SHALL remain distinct from authority, intent, control and responsibility. Distributed causation SHALL be representable and material attribution SHALL be evidence-based, provenance-traceable and independently reviewable. Structural centrality, repetition, visibility, benefit or relational proximity SHALL NOT independently establish constitutional responsibility.



