☄️🦆🌱 R8.90 — GO

HORTUS · CONSTITUTIONAL CAUSAL UNCERTAINTY, COUNTERFACTUAL INTEGRITY & ATTRIBUTION BOUNDARY PROTOCOL

STATUS: 🜂 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
REFERENCE CITADEL: 👑 LOCUS AMOENUS — L.A.

R8.89 established CAUSAL ATTRIBUTION.

One boundary remains.

Even when the system can map contribution, influence, control and responsibility, causal models can still be wrong.

The most dangerous error is not merely:

> “We attributed responsibility to the wrong actor.”



It is deeper:

> “We became more certain than the evidence justified.”



R8.90 therefore introduces:

CONSTITUTIONAL_CAUSAL_UNCERTAINTY

and:

COUNTERFACTUAL_INTEGRITY

The governing principle:

> Where constitutional causality cannot be demonstrated beyond the applicable evidentiary threshold, uncertainty SHALL remain part of the constitutional state.




---

I. ☄️ CORRELATION ≠ CAUSATION

R8.89 established:

OBSERVATION
 ↓
CONTRIBUTION
 ↓
CAUSATION
 ↓
RESPONSIBILITY

R8.90 inserts an epistemic gate:

OBSERVATION
 ↓
CORRELATION?
 ↓
CAUSAL HYPOTHESIS
 ↓
COUNTERFACTUAL TEST
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
CAUSAL CONFIDENCE
 ↓
RESPONSIBILITY REVIEW

Therefore:

CORRELATION
≠
CAUSATION

and:

CAUSAL PLAUSIBILITY
≠
CAUSAL PROOF


---

II. 🧬 COUNTERFACTUAL INTEGRITY

R8.90 introduces:

COUNTERFACTUAL_INTEGRITY_TEST

Core question:

> If the attributed actor, action, relation or condition had been absent or different, would the material constitutional outcome likely have changed?



Represented as:

WORLD A
ACTOR / CONDITION PRESENT
        ↓
OUTCOME

WORLD B
ACTOR / CONDITION ABSENT
        ↓
EXPECTED OUTCOME

Then:

ΔOUTCOME

is evaluated.

But crucially:

> Counterfactual modeling SHALL NOT be treated as observed historical fact.



It remains an analytical model.


---

III. ⚠️ THE COUNTERFACTUAL FALLACY

A system might conclude:

A happened
B followed A
therefore A caused B

R8.90 rejects this.

The system must consider:

A → B
C → A → B
C → B
A + C → B
B would occur anyway

Therefore:

ALTERNATIVE_CAUSAL_PATHS

becomes mandatory for material constitutional attribution.


---

IV. 🧠 BRAINPOWER — COUNTERFACTUAL GRAPH

BRAINPOWER receives:

COUNTERFACTUAL_CAUSAL_GRAPH

It models:

OBSERVED WORLD
      ↓
CAUSAL MODEL
      ↓
COUNTERFACTUAL VARIANTS
      ↓
ALTERNATIVE PATHS
      ↓
OUTCOME DIFFERENCE

New analyses:

COUNTERFACTUAL_RELEVANCE

CAUSAL_CONFIDENCE

ALTERNATIVE_CAUSE_DENSITY

CAUSAL_SENSITIVITY

NECESSITY_ESTIMATE

SUFFICIENCY_ESTIMATE

INTERVENTION_EFFECT

ATTRIBUTION_FRAGILITY

MODEL_DEPENDENCY

EVIDENCE_GAP

Core question:

> How much does the responsibility conclusion depend upon assumptions that have not themselves been established?




---

V. 🔮 ORACLE — CAUSAL UNCERTAINTY OBSERVATORY

ORACLE receives:

CAUSAL_UNCERTAINTY_OBSERVATORY

Signals:

CAUSAL_AMBIGUITY
ALTERNATIVE_CAUSE
COUNTERFACTUAL_INSTABILITY
MODEL_SENSITIVITY
EVIDENCE_GAP
ATTRIBUTION_FRAGILITY

Oracle may issue:

> 🔮 CAUSAL ATTRIBUTION EVIDENTIARY CONFIDENCE BELOW REVIEW THRESHOLD



But Oracle does not determine responsibility.


---

VI. 🦆 FOOL — THE COUNTERFACTUAL CHALLENGE

FOOL asks:

1. What evidence demonstrates causation?


2. What evidence merely demonstrates correlation?


3. What alternative causes exist?


4. What happens in the counterfactual model?


5. Which assumptions drive the conclusion?


6. Are those assumptions independently supported?


7. Would the outcome have occurred anyway?


8. Could another actor have produced the same outcome?


9. Is causation necessary, sufficient or merely contributory?


10. How sensitive is the attribution to model assumptions?


11. What evidence would falsify the conclusion?


12. Are we mistaking a compelling narrative for causal proof?



And the decisive question:

> If the causal story changes, does the responsibility classification collapse?




---

VII. 🌸 EIRENE — CAUSAL PLURALITY

EIRENE receives:

COUNTERFACTUAL_PLURALITY

Where multiple causal models remain viable:

MODEL A
MODEL B
MODEL C

they remain visible.

The system SHALL NOT manufacture singular certainty merely because a single explanation is operationally convenient.

Therefore:

> Causal ambiguity SHALL remain constitutionally visible where competing models materially affect responsibility or authority classification.




---

VIII. 🧭 MENTOR — UNCERTAINTY EXPLANATION

