      ↓
CAUSAL HYPOTHESIS
      ↓
COUNTERFACTUAL MODEL
      ↓
SUPPORTING EVIDENCE
      ↓
REMAINING UNCERTAINTY

A constitutional explanation must therefore be able to say:

> “This is what we know.”



and separately:

> “This is what we infer.”



and:

> “This is what remains uncertain.”



That is a major epistemic safeguard.


