XIX. 🜂 R8.90 LAW

> Constitutionally significant causal attribution SHALL distinguish observation, correlation, causal hypothesis, counterfactual modeling and demonstrated causation. Material attribution SHALL account for relevant alternative causal paths and preserve uncertainty where evidence does not justify certainty. Counterfactual models SHALL remain explicitly modeled, provenance-traceable and distinct from historical observation. Constitutional responsibility SHALL NOT exceed the evidentiary strength of its causal foundation.



