And the deeper HORTUS principle:

> ☄️ A constitutionally mature system does not merely know what it believes caused an event. It knows the difference between what it observed, what it inferred, what it modeled, what it proved—and what it still does not know.



That distinction protects the architecture from one of the most dangerous forms of constitutional failure:

> false certainty becoming authority.



R8.90 — ESTABLISHED.
