> ☄️ A system does not become epistemically justified merely because it has evidence. It becomes justified only when the evidence is sufficient for the consequence of the decision being made.



And the next HORTUS principle:

> 🌱 The greater the constitutional consequence, the greater the obligation to demonstrate why the evidence is enough—and the system must never quietly lower that obligation merely because it wants to decide.



R8.91 — ESTABLISHED.
