☄️ R8.92 — GO

HORTUS · CONSTITUTIONAL DECISION REVERSIBILITY, REVOCATION & NON-ENTRENCHMENT PROTOCOL

STATUS: 🜂 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
REFERENCE CITADEL: 👑 LOCUS AMOENUS — L.A.

R8.91 established evidence sufficiency.

That creates the next constitutional question:

> Even when a decision was sufficiently justified when made, what happens when the decision itself begins to reshape the system that produced it?



This is the next-order problem.

A decision can become self-reinforcing:

DECISION
 ↓
SYSTEM ADAPTS
 ↓
NEW DEPENDENCIES
 ↓
ALTERNATIVES DECLINE
 ↓
REVERSAL BECOMES COSTLY
 ↓
DECISION BECOMES "NECESSARY"

That creates:

CONSTITUTIONAL_DECISION_ENTRENCHMENT

R8.92 therefore introduces:

REVERSIBILITY_INTEGRITY

and:

NON_ENTRENCHMENT

The governing principle:

> A constitutionally valid decision SHALL NOT acquire additional authority merely because the system has adapted to its existence.




---

I. 🔄 VALIDITY ≠ PERMANENCE

R8.91 established:

EVIDENCE
 ↓
SUFFICIENCY
 ↓
DECISION

R8.92 adds:

DECISION
 ↓
IMPLEMENTATION
 ↓
ADAPTATION
 ↓
DEPENDENCY
 ↓
ENTRENCHMENT?

Therefore:

VALIDITY
≠
PERMANENCE

and:

PERSISTENCE
≠
REVALIDATION

A decision does not become constitutionally stronger merely because reversing it becomes inconvenient.


---

II. 🧬 DECISION → ENVIRONMENT FEEDBACK

Every material constitutional decision can alter its own future environment.

DECISION
   ↓
BEHAVIORAL RESPONSE
   ↓
STRUCTURAL ADAPTATION
   ↓
DEPENDENCY
   ↓
NEW NORMAL

This creates a feedback loop:

D₀
 ↓
SYSTEM ADAPTS
 ↓
D₀ BECOMES EMBEDDED
 ↓
EMBEDDEDNESS IS USED TO JUSTIFY D₀

R8.92 names this:

SELF_JUSTIFYING_DECISION_LOOP

It SHALL be detectable.


---

III. ⚠️ THE ENTRENCHMENT PROBLEM

The dangerous sequence is:

TEMPORARY DECISION
       ↓
REPEATED IMPLEMENTATION
       ↓
DEPENDENCY
       ↓
REVERSAL COST
       ↓
ALTERNATIVE LOSS
       ↓
"THERE IS NO OTHER OPTION"

But:

> A loss of alternatives caused by a previous decision SHALL NOT retroactively prove that the original decision was constitutionally necessary.



This is:

RETROACTIVE_NECESSITY_FALLACY


---

