> A constitutional reversal SHALL preserve historical lineage while transitioning the system toward a validated successor state. Transitional mechanisms and temporary authorities SHALL remain explicitly bounded, provenance-traceable and subject to independent review. No temporary authority SHALL acquire constitutional legitimacy through persistence, necessity or convenience. A reversal SHALL not be considered constitutionally complete until the resulting state satisfies the applicable validation threshold.



