> Operational continuity SHALL NOT independently establish constitutional identity continuity. Where cumulative transformation materially alters authority, jurisdiction, roles, boundaries, identity or constitutional relationships, the system SHALL determine whether the resulting state remains constitutionally continuous or constitutes a new constitutional identity. Such determination SHALL remain evidence-based, historically traceable, independently reviewable and resistant to shadow reconstitution.



