☄️ R9.07 — GO

HORTUS · CONSTITUTIONAL UNCERTAINTY, EPISTEMIC RESERVE & DECISION INTEGRITY PROTOCOL

STATUS: 🜂 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
REFERENCE CITADEL: 👑 LOCUS AMOENUS — L.A.

R9.06 established that constitutional memory can remain conflicted without being erased.

That creates the next unavoidable question:

> What may a constitutional system legitimately do when it does not know enough?



A dangerous system converts uncertainty into certainty.

A brittle system refuses to act.

A constitutional system needs a third state:

UNCERTAINTY
↓
BOUNDED ACTION
↓
PRESERVED REVIEWABILITY

R9.07 therefore introduces:

CONSTITUTIONAL_UNCERTAINTY

and:

EPISTEMIC_RESERVE

The central principle:

> Unknown SHALL remain unknown until sufficient evidence justifies a stronger classification.




---

I. 🔮 UNCERTAINTY ≠ IGNORANCE

R9.07 distinguishes:

UNKNOWN
≠
UNCERTAIN
≠
DISPUTED
≠
INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE
≠
CONTESTED_INTERPRETATION

These states have different constitutional meanings.

UNKNOWN

No sufficiently reliable information is available.

UNCERTAIN

Evidence exists, but does not establish one conclusion with sufficient confidence.

DISPUTED

Multiple materially relevant claims remain active.

INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE

The available evidence cannot support the required decision threshold.

CONTESTED_INTERPRETATION

Evidence may be established while its constitutional meaning remains disputed.

This prevents epistemic states from collapsing into one generic:

> “We don't know.”




---

II. 🧬 THE EPISTEMIC CHAIN

R9.07 establishes:

OBSERVATION
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
PROVENANCE
 ↓
ASSESSMENT
 ↓
CONFIDENCE
 ↓
UNCERTAINTY
 ↓
DECISION THRESHOLD
 ↓
