 ↓
REVERSIBILITY
 ↓
TEMPORAL LIMIT
 ↓
ACTION
 ↓
REVIEW

A high-impact irreversible action should require a substantially stronger evidentiary basis than a low-impact reversible action.

This creates:

EVIDENCE_TO_AUTHORITY_PROPORTIONALITY

The principle:

> The greater the constitutional consequence, the stronger the required epistemic basis.




