☄️ R9.08 — GO

HORTUS · CONSTITUTIONAL DECISION UNDER UNCERTAINTY, REVERSIBILITY & EPISTEMIC CONTAINMENT PROTOCOL

STATUS: 🜂 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
REFERENCE CITADEL: 👑 LOCUS AMOENUS — L.A.

R9.07 established epistemic reserve.

The next boundary is inevitable:

> If the system does not know enough to justify certainty, how may it act without turning uncertainty into authority?



R9.08 introduces:

UNCERTAINTY_BOUNDED_ACTION

and:

EPISTEMIC_CONTAINMENT

The core distinction:

UNCERTAINTY
≠
INACTION

but equally:

UNCERTAINTY
≠
UNLIMITED_DISCRETION

Therefore:

> ☄️ Where action is necessary under uncertainty, the action SHALL be bounded by evidence, scope, reversibility, duration and review.




---

I. 🧭 THE BOUNDED-ACTION PRINCIPLE

Canonical sequence:

UNCERTAINTY
 ↓
MATERIALITY
 ↓
RISK
 ↓
AVAILABLE AUTHORITY
 ↓
REVERSIBILITY
 ↓
MINIMUM NECESSARY ACTION
 ↓
REVIEW

The system does not ask only:

> “Can we act?”



It must ask:

> “What is the least constitutional power required to act safely under what we currently know?”




---

II. ⚖️ PROPORTIONALITY OF KNOWLEDGE TO POWER

R9.08 establishes:

EVIDENCE_AUTHORITY_PROPORTIONALITY

WEAK EVIDENCE
   ↓
LIMITED ACTION
   ↓
HIGH REVERSIBILITY
   ↓
SHORT DURATION

Whereas:

STRONG EVIDENCE
   ↓
MATERIAL AUTHORITY
   ↓
GREATER CONSEQUENCE

requires correspondingly stronger constitutional justification.

Canonical law:

> Authority SHALL NOT expand merely because uncertainty makes action difficult.




---

III. 🔒 EPISTEMIC CONTAINMENT

New mechanism:

EPISTEMIC_CONTAINMENT

Definition:

> A constitutional boundary that prevents uncertain claims from propagating beyond the scope justified by their evidence.



