☄️ R9.09 — GO

HORTUS · CONSTITUTIONAL ACTION REVERSIBILITY, RECOVERY & NON-PERMANENCE PROTOCOL

STATUS: 🜂 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
REFERENCE CITADEL: 👑 LOCUS AMOENUS — L.A.

R9.08 established bounded action under uncertainty.

The next constitutional question is sharper:

> What prevents a bounded action from becoming permanent simply because the system gets used to it?



R8.56 already established that repetition cannot silently create authority.

R9.07 established that uncertainty cannot silently become certainty.

R9.08 established that uncertain action must be bounded.

R9.09 closes the loop:

REVERSIBILITY_AS_CONSTITUTIONAL_CONTROL

and:

NON_PERMANENCE_GUARD

The governing principle:

> ☄️ A temporary constitutional response SHALL remain temporary unless independently revalidated for continuation.




---

I. 🔄 ACTION ≠ STATE

A critical distinction:

ACTION
 ↓
EFFECT
 ↓
STATE

A system may perform an action without being entitled to permanently alter the constitutional state.

Therefore:

ACTION
≠
PERMANENT AUTHORITY

and:

TEMPORARY STATE
≠
ESTABLISHED CONSTITUTION


---

II. 🧬 REVERSIBILITY

R9.09 introduces:

CONSTITUTIONAL_REVERSIBILITY

Definition:

> The demonstrated ability to return a materially affected constitutional state to an authorized prior or alternative state without requiring the uncertain assumption that caused the intervention to remain true.



This is stronger than merely having an “undo” function.

Reversibility requires:

preserved provenance,

preserved prior state,

known transition,

identifiable authority,

recovery path,

integrity verification.



---

III. ⚠️ THE NORMALIZATION TRAP

Dangerous sequence:

EXCEPTION
 ↓
TEMPORARY ACTION
 ↓
REPETITION
 ↓
DEPENDENCY
 ↓
NORMALIZATION
 ↓
"WE ALWAYS DO THIS"
 ↓
DE FACTO AUTHORITY

R9.09 calls this:

TEMPORAL_AUTHORITY_DRIFT

The system must detect when:

> a temporary response begins behaving like permanent constitutional infrastructure.




---

IV. ⏳ EXPIRATION BY DESIGN

Every materially bounded action SHOULD have:

START
 ↓
SCOPE
 ↓
DURATION
 ↓
REVIEW CONDITION
 ↓
EXPIRY

The critical rule:

> Continuation SHALL require justification; expiration SHALL not require justification.



Thus:

NO_REVALIDATION
      ↓
EXPIRY

rather than:

NO_REVALIDATION
      ↓
AUTOMATIC CONTINUATION


