VIII. 🦆 FOOL — THE PERMANENCE CHALLENGE

FOOL asks:

1. Was this action intended to be temporary?


2. When does it expire?


3. Who benefits from continuation?


4. Has anyone become dependent upon it?


5. Have alternatives disappeared?


6. Has reversal become more expensive?


7. Has an exception become normal?


8. Has authority silently persisted?


9. What independent basis justifies continuation?


10. Could the system still return to the prior state?



Core question:

> If nobody explicitly renewed this authority, why does it still exist?




