→
PLURALITY

Loss of reversibility can cause loss of legitimate alternatives.

Therefore:

> Constitutional interventions SHOULD preserve future legitimate options wherever practicable.



A system that cannot reverse itself can eventually become trapped by its own temporary decisions.


